From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: correct SDM660 GPU source rate and parent

The imported gfx3d clock op promises 19.2 MHz for the GPU's 27 MHz idle
request, but fails to update the rounded request rate. It also leaves
best_parent_hw unchanged when the bootloader selected GCC GPU GPLL0.
Report the actual idle rate and choose GPU PLL0 for that parent.

Fixes: f806ce1da3da ("clk: qcom: rcg2: Add new gfx3d_src ops for SDM630/660 GPUCC")
Source-Commit: https://github.com/sdm660-mainline/linux/commit/f806ce1da3dabc5e045308a8444bbd0c4077b484
Scope: SDM630/660-common
Porting notes: Local migration review correction; 0018 retains the original source hunk.
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rcg2.c
@@ -1339,7 +1339,7 @@
 	if (req->rate < 30000000) {
 		req->best_parent_hw = xo;
 		/* return 19.2 MHz even for 27 MHz requests */
-		req->best_parent_rate = clk_hw_get_rate(xo);
+		req->rate = req->best_parent_rate = clk_hw_get_rate(xo);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
@@ -1355,10 +1355,7 @@
 
 	parent_req.rate = f->freq * (f->pre_div + 1) / 2;
 
-	if (curr_p == xo || curr_p == p1)
-		req->best_parent_hw = p0;
-	else if (curr_p == p0)
-		req->best_parent_hw = p1;
+	req->best_parent_hw = curr_p == p0 ? p1 : p0;
 
 	parent_req.best_parent_hw = clk_hw_get_parent(req->best_parent_hw);
 	parent_req.best_parent_rate = clk_hw_get_rate(parent_req.best_parent_hw);
